From: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
Subject: [TEST] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: wait for SDS indirect write completion

Proposed on the OpenWrt forum (reduce-number-of-drivers-for-rtl8367s #70)
as a candidate fix for the cold-start degraded HSGMII trunk seen on the
TP-Link Archer AX55 v1: back-to-back SDS_INDACS writes (SerDes tuning
jam tables) may race when the SerDes PLL is cold after a hard reset.
Mirror the BUSY-bit poll that rtl8365mb_sds_read() already does.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -1161,6 +1161,7 @@
 
 static int rtl8365mb_sds_write(struct realtek_priv *priv, u16 addr, u16 data)
 {
+	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = regmap_write(priv->map, RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_DATA_REG, data);
@@ -1171,13 +1172,22 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* The SerDes indirect access engine completes the command within the
-	 * register write transaction, so there is no need to wait or poll for
-	 * completion before the next access, matching the vendor driver.
+	ret = regmap_write(priv->map, RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_REG,
+			   RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_RUN_MASK |
+			   RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_WR_MASK);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Wait for the indirect write to complete, mirroring
+	 * rtl8365mb_sds_read(): the engine clears the BUSY bit once the
+	 * write has actually landed. Back-to-back writes can otherwise
+	 * race the previous one, especially when the SerDes PLL is cold
+	 * after a hard reset.
 	 */
-	return regmap_write(priv->map, RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_REG,
-			    RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_RUN_MASK |
-			    RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_WR_MASK);
+	return regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->map,
+					RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_REG, val,
+					!(val & RTL8365MB_SDS_INDACS_CMD_BUSY_MASK),
+					10, 1000);
 }
 
 static int rtl8365mb_sds_read(struct realtek_priv *priv, u16 addr, u16 *data)
